course: dictionary
lesson: 15973
title: Unwrap: taking off the cover
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To unwrap something is to take off the paper, plastic or cover that is around it. The prefix un- often means the reverse of an action, so unwrap is the opposite of wrap. «Mia carefully unwrapped her birthday present.» Mia took the paper off, so she could see the gift inside.
explain: Unwrap can also mean to reveal or explain something that was hidden or hard to understand. This is informal, so you will meet it more in talk and stories than in formal writing. «The teacher unwrapped the idea so everyone could follow it.» The teacher made the idea clear, the way you would open up a package to show what is inside.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Is someone holding a present, a sweet or a sandwich? Then it means take off the cover. Is someone explaining a puzzle, a plan or a secret? Then it means reveal or explain. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
fact: Unwrap is a verb. Its forms are unwrap, unwraps, unwrapped and unwrapping.
fact: «Unwrap» means to take off the paper, plastic or cover around something.
fact: The prefix «un-» often shows the reverse of an action, so unwrap is the opposite of wrap.
fact: Informally, «unwrap» can mean to reveal or explain something hidden, such as a secret or an idea.
fact: You can unwrap presents, sweets, sandwiches and parcels, and a detective can unwrap a mystery.
exercise: «Mia carefully unwrapped her birthday present.» What does unwrapped mean here? | Hid it under the bed | *Took off the paper around it | Broke it into pieces | Put a bow on it
exercise: «The teacher unwrapped the idea so everyone could follow it.» What does unwrapped mean here? | Wrapped it up even tighter | Forgot it completely | *Explained it clearly | Threw it away
exercise: Find and copy the word that means took the paper off in this sentence: «Dad unwrapped a sandwich in the car.» | car | sandwich | Dad | *unwrapped
test: «The detective unwrapped the mystery, step by step.» What does unwrapped mean here? | Ignored the mystery | Solved it by magic | Took the paper off the mystery | *Explained the mystery bit by bit
test: Which word is the opposite of wrap in meaning? | rapped | wrapper | wrapping | *unwrap
exam: Which is the best way to check the meaning of unwrap in a new sentence? | Skip the sentence and never come back to it | *Swap in a meaning like take the cover off, and see if it still makes sense | Guess the longest word in the sentence | Count the letters in the word
